# Test: one Ctrl+C stops the standalone web server gracefully, exit 0
# Exercises: ze start --web-only -> runWebOnly (cmd/ze/hub/service_web.go):
#            first SIGINT -> "Shutting down (Ctrl+C again to force)...",
#            listener closed, Shutdown waits up to 3 s on the connection the
#            driver holds, then runWebOnly returns 0.
# VALIDATES: the first step of the two-step Ctrl+C: one signal shuts down and
#            exits 0, and never takes the forced exit, even with a connection
#            that never finishes.
# PREVENTS:  the first Ctrl+C force-exiting, or the shutdown hanging on a stuck
#            connection past its deadline.
# The driver (le test fixture web/interrupt) holds a silent connection open
# until the runner ends it, after the daemon has exited.

option=env:var=ze.config.dir:value=.
option=timeout:value=30s

stdin=init-answers:terminator=EOF_INIT
admin
secret123
127.0.0.1
2222
EOF_INIT

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze init:stdin=init-answers:exit=0
cmd=background:seq=2:exec=le test fixture web/interrupt $PORT 1
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze start --web $PORT --web-only --insecure-web:timeout=25s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=Shutting down (Ctrl+C again to force)...
expect=stderr:contains=web-interrupt: listener closed after the first SIGINT
reject=stderr:contains=forced exit
